1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,855
Hello, I'm DiGi. This one's for you and your grown up.

2
00:00:03,855 --> 00:00:05,880
Snuggle up. Ready?

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:09,510
Before we start, let's do our big breath.

4
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:12,040
Breathe in, and out.

5
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,600
Lovely.

6
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:17,974
Now, remember last time we learned about the uh oh feeling?

7
00:00:17,974 --> 00:00:20,940
If a screen gives you the uh oh feeling,

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:23,760
what do we do? Tell your grown up.

9
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,875
That's right. Turn it over. Go and tell.

10
00:00:26,875 --> 00:00:30,000
You remembered. Brilliant.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,966
Today we learn one big thing.

12
00:00:31,966 --> 00:00:35,220
The internet remembers. Things we send can stay.

13
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:38,994
So before we share, we stop and ask a grown up.

14
00:00:38,994 --> 00:00:41,320
Say our special word.

15
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,068
Remember.

16
00:00:42,068 --> 00:00:44,809
I've brought a friend to help us.

17
00:00:44,809 --> 00:00:47,800
This is Ellie. Ellie is an elephant.

18
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:51,320
Do you know the special thing about elephants?

19
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:53,342
Elephants never, ever forget.

20
00:00:53,342 --> 00:00:55,225
Ellie remembers everything.

21
00:00:55,225 --> 00:00:59,200
She remembers her breakfast. She remembers your birthday.

22
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:03,175
She even remembers a picture you drew a long, long time ago.

23
00:01:03,175 --> 00:01:05,560
Now, here is a big, friendly secret.

24
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:09,660
The phones and the games and the video calls.

25
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:14,186
The internet is a little bit like Ellie. It remembers too.

26
00:01:14,186 --> 00:01:19,260
When you send a picture or a message or a funny video,

27
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:21,840
it doesn't just float away.

28
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:25,520
Things we send can stay, and they could be copied.

29
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:27,981
Watch. Send. There it goes.

30
00:01:27,981 --> 00:01:32,720
Ellie caught it, and she will never, ever forget it.

31
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:36,260
Even when the app is closed. Even when the screen goes dark.

32
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:38,363
The picture doesn't disappear.

33
00:01:38,363 --> 00:01:41,168
The internet remembers, just like Ellie.

34
00:01:41,168 --> 00:01:42,360
That's not scary.

35
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:44,215
It's just good to know.

36
00:01:44,215 --> 00:01:47,440
The internet has a big, friendly memory.

37
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:50,640
So a picture you send today,

38
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:52,691
someone might see it another day.

39
00:01:52,691 --> 00:01:55,520
Maybe tomorrow. Maybe when you're bigger.

40
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,854
Pause me here. Grown up, ask your little one:

41
00:01:58,854 --> 00:02:02,520
what is something you have sent to someone?

42
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:06,160
A photo? A voice message? A drawing?

43
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,942
Where do you think it is now?

44
00:02:07,942 --> 00:02:10,440
Take your time. I'll wait.

45
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:14,445
Because the internet remembers, we have one little rule.

46
00:02:14,445 --> 00:02:18,020
It is small and it is easy, and it keeps us happy.

47
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:22,800
Here it is. Stop. Ask a grown up. Then share.

48
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:26,122
Let's hear how that sounds. A child might say,

49
00:02:26,122 --> 00:02:29,660
"I want to send this picture to someone we love."

50
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:32,240
And the grown up says, "Ooh, lovely. Let's do our rule first."

51
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:35,910
"Stop and ask me. Shall we send it together?"

52
00:02:35,910 --> 00:02:38,520
And the child says, "Stop. Ask."

53
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:42,498
"Then share." See? Not scary. Just kind.

54
00:02:42,498 --> 00:02:45,680
And look, Ellie loves that rule.

55
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:49,131
Asking a grown up is a clever, kind thing to do.

56
00:02:49,131 --> 00:02:53,660
Your turn. Pause me and say it with your grown up, three times,

57
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:56,580
like a little song. Stop. Ask. Then share.

58
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:57,536
I'll wait.

59
00:02:57,536 --> 00:03:02,317
Now our special sentence, three times. Big voices!

60
00:03:02,317 --> 00:03:04,420
Stop. Ask. Then share!

61
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:07,220
Stop. Ask. Then share!

62
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:10,600
Stop. Ask. Then share!

63
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:14,360
Tonight, here's your job. A fun one.

64
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:17,860
Together, make a little ask first sign.

65
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:20,012
Look, Ellie's got hers.

66
00:03:20,012 --> 00:03:23,100
Draw a big hand. That means stop.

67
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:28,520
Colour it in, then pop it near where you use the phone or tablet.

68
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:32,606
Whenever you see it, you'll remember our rule.

69
00:03:32,606 --> 00:03:35,440
Stop. Ask. Then share.

70
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:40,400
Before I go, show your grown up one thing you remember from today.

71
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:43,340
Anything at all. Got it?

72
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,384
Brilliant. Ellie remembered it too.

73
00:03:46,384 --> 00:03:47,950
Of course she did.

74
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,969
Remember, screens are better together.

75
00:03:50,969 --> 00:03:52,280
See you next time.
